  "term": "microglia",
  "definition": "Microglia are a type of glial cell in the central nervous system, distinct from the macroglia such as astrocytes and oligodendrocytes. Their form can differ by developmental stage, location, and activity, and they can engulf material, contribute to immune-related functions, and help with nervous system development, remodeling, and disease processes.",
